 USA Inc., together with subsidiaries, engages in marketing of retail motor fuel products and convenience merchandise. The company operates retail stores under the Murphy USA, Murphy Express, and QuickChek brands, as well as operates non-fuel convenience stores. It operates retail gasoline stores principally in the Southeast, Southwest, and Midwest areas of the United States. Murphy USA Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in El Dorado, Arkansas.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Malynda K. West CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $3.3M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $63K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Murphy USA Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $9.4B market cap on $19.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $374M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.73\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 10.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here's Why Murphy USA (MUSA) is a Strong Value Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025453/here-s-why-murphy-usa-musa-is-a-strong-value-stock?c