he 5% durability bar.","Capex runs 1.6x depreciation (2.3% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 13, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 17.8% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 10.0%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 90%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (8 sales, net $5.9M sold).","It returns 7.3% a year to shareholders (6.9% in buybacks and 0.6% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 7.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 5,900 employees, each generates about $3.3M of revenue, 8.6x the Consumer Cyclical median.","That works out to $63K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.7M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":83,"head":"Invest: trades 27% below fair value of $716; ROIC 23.4% vs WACC 7.0%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 50, gates 13/26)","Trades 27% below fair value of $716","ROIC 23.4% vs WACC 7.0%","Revenue grew 11.5%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["P/FCF 25.2x vs sector 16.5x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":608.3,"vc":{"base":715.65,"base_src":"dcf","bear":502.32,"bull":1040.23,"alt_median":366.67,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.9517,"dispersion":0.3862,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (39% dispersion)","DCF is 95% above the other models' median ($367)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"MUSA","date":"2026-11-06"}